    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression \\(2x + 5\\).\n2. Calculate the value of \\(2x + 5\\).\n3. Square the result from step 2.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 3\\) into \\(2x + 5\\):\n   \\[\n   2(3) + 5\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the value of \\(2(3) + 5\\):\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 3 + 5 = 6 + 5 = 11\n   \\]\n\n3. Square the result from step 2:\n   \\[\n   11^2 = 11 \\cdot 11 = 121\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).",
