    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression \\(2x + 5\\).\n2. Simplify the expression inside the parentheses.\n3. Square the result.\n\nLet's start with the substitution:\n\n\\[2x + 5 = 2(3) + 5\\]\n\nNext, we perform the multiplication:\n\n\\[2(3) + 5 = 6 + 5\\]\n\nThen, we add the numbers:\n\n\\[6 + 5 = 11\\]\n\nSo, the expression \\(2x + 5\\) evaluates to 11 when \\(x = 3\\). Now, we need to square this result:\n\n\\[(2x + 5)^2 = 11^2\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate the square of 11:\n\n\\[11^2 = 121\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).",
